{#
  "Log out?" — rendered by LogoutController. LogoutRequestGuard redirects here
  when the logout path is reached any way other than the logout button: an old
  bookmark, a stale tab, a typed URL, or a form whose security token expired.
  Signed-out visitors never see it; the controller sends them home.

  The page must NOT read as though logout happened, because it has not. On a
  shared computer, someone who sees "you're logged out" and walks away leaves
  their session open. So the heading is a question and the first sentence says
  plainly that they are still signed in.

  Variables:
    expired  bool  TRUE when a logout form was submitted with a missing or
                   expired token (served as 403); FALSE for a plain visit.

  @see \Pixiekat\HMFPSearchToolBundle\Controller\LogoutController
  @see \Pixiekat\HMFPSearchToolBundle\EventListener\LogoutRequestGuard
#}
{% extends '@HMFPSearchTool/search/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block search_page_title %}Log out?{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <section class="logout-confirm" aria-labelledby="logout-confirm-heading">
    <h2 id="logout-confirm-heading">Log out?</h2>

    {% if expired %}
      <p>
        <strong>You have not been logged out yet.</strong>
        The page you used had been open for a while and its security check ran out.
        Please use the button below to log out.
      </p>
    {% else %}
      <p><strong>You are still logged in.</strong> To log out, use the button below.</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% include '@HMFPSearchTool/security/_logout_form.html.twig' with { button_class: 'button' } %}

    <p><a href="{{ path('hmfp_search_tool_home') }}">Stay logged in and go back to search</a></p>
  </section>
{% endblock %}
